WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.700
- Before Joe Rogan was a hit podcast host,

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.860
and after Ludacris was a hit rapper,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.080
they were hosts of a show
called, "Fear Factor."

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.670
Do not try any of these at home.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.240
I'm watching for medical
accuracy and information only.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.073
Pew.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.865
Oh, oh my God.

00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:19.830
(horror music)
Worst fear alert of my life.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.530
Oh my God forget about
the little pinchers.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.585
The tail just going...

00:00:23.585 --> 00:00:24.876
(bouncing)

00:00:24.876 --> 00:00:25.929
(squishing)

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:27.570
- Calm down, calm down, calm down.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.668
- Oh my God, she has to put them in there?

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:32.520
(horror music)
They're biting her hand, no!

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.670
If aliens were ever to come
down to Earth and see this,

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.470
they would feel pity on us.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.870
- [Joe] One of you will
be bound by your wrists,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.277
while covered in over 100,000 bees.

00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:44.435
- A hundred thousand...

00:00:44.435 --> 00:00:47.670
- [Joe] Your partner is going
to have to eat 20 live bees.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.863
- I'm more afraid for the bees.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.170
What did the bees do to deserve this?

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.820
Oh my God, I would have a full,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.653
forget panic attack,

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:55.486
this is dangerous.

00:00:55.486 --> 00:00:56.319
Getting stung by bees

00:00:56.319 --> 00:00:58.200
causes localized inflammatory response.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.171
If you have an anaphylactic
reaction, you could die.

00:01:00.171 --> 00:01:02.310
(woman screaming)

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.523
- [Joe] Alright, here comes
the first bee down the hatch.

00:01:03.523 --> 00:01:05.520
- Oh my God, what happens
when you eat a bee?

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.186
Can it sting you or are
those stingless bees?

00:01:08.186 --> 00:01:09.677
(chopping)

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:10.860
- [Joe] That's it, nice.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.050
- Okay, she's not out of harm's way yet.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.948
It's not nice.

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:15.030
(buzzing)

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.140
How do you get them off of her?

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.010
Did she get stung?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.970
Show me a sting.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.460
- [Man] They didn't show
removing them entirely.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.720
- Huh? I wonder.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.973
I wonder if those were stingless bees.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.483
Oh no, being submerged.

00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:27.960
Worse feeling ever.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.000
These challenges always
scare the life out of me.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.260
Cause if they like, drown,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.300
they're gonna need life-support quick.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.890
And remember, when you're
doing chest compressions

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.910
on someone who's drowning,

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.650
very different than
doing chest compressions

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.120
for people who are on land.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.010
You only need to do hands-only CPR,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.330
if you find someone down on land.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.250
But drowning, you need
to give rescue breaths.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:45.720
Start with rescue breaths.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.653
- [Ludacris] Hold on, Marisa's in trouble.

00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:47.820
Marisa's in trouble.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.111
- Breathe!
- Oh no.

00:01:49.111 --> 00:01:50.700
- [Ludacris] Breathe!

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.320
They are struggling to breathe.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.153
- Yeah, it's hard to breathe,

00:01:53.153 --> 00:01:55.560
cause all the little things
are going in your mouth.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.600
- [Ludacris] That's two more wing nuts.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.530
- She's just breathing.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.300
She's not even participating in the task.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.477
She's like, I'm just gonna live here.

00:02:02.477 --> 00:02:04.500
- Oh (beep), oh (beep),
oh (beep), oh (beep).

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.333
- Oh, this is scary.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:06.166
- I'm literally jumping off a bridge.

00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:07.110
- What's about to happen?

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.880
- [Woman] I get like a little anxious,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:09.930
like if I do look down.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.900
- Normal human emotion,
this is not a phobia!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.790
You're hanging off like a spider,

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.290
at the bottom of a helicopter,

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.130
and you're afraid.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.060
Normal fear.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.617
Nothing medically wrong with this.

00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:21.075
(intense music)

00:02:21.075 --> 00:02:22.140
(cheering)

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.310
- [Ludacris] Now she's
going for the ripcord.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.423
She got the last knot.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.773
(woman screaming)

00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:30.900
- Oh what, is a bungee
jump off a helicopter?

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.950
That feels dangerous.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.198
Can you imagine if she just like,

00:02:33.198 --> 00:02:34.031
(bouncing)

00:02:34.031 --> 00:02:36.690
bungee jumped all the
way over the helicopter,

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.590
onto the blades.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.210
That would've been evil.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.440
Bungee jumping is dangerous.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.050
Because that recoil can cause
like snapping of the neck,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:43.980
if it's not secure,

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.380
and you know, snapping of
the neck is never ideal.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:51.380
- Inside this box, are
over 500 bull testicles.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.210
- I watched this episode with my parents

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.070
when we came as immigrants from Russia.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.110
And we were like, what
is happening in America?

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.860
- On go, your partner is
gonna smash their face

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.307
into this box of testicles.

00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:05.010
(laughing)

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.600
- On nationwide television,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.640
your partner has to smash their face

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.200
into a box of testicles.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.000
I don't even know if
there's any harm here,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:12.833
like medically.

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.580
What if the cow had an STI?

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.750
Maybe that could be a problem.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.580
Like an epididymitis.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.800
Hmm, this is what an
epididymitis looks like.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.633
- [Joe] Your partner,

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.710
will then have to spit out that testicle

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.551
into the testicle receptacle.

00:03:24.551 --> 00:03:25.384
(record scratching)

00:03:25.384 --> 00:03:26.640
- (laughs) Who made?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.412
What five year old made this stunt?

00:03:28.412 --> 00:03:31.050
(intense music)

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.365
- [Joe] All right, Missy,
she's got a testicle.

00:03:32.365 --> 00:03:33.840
(water splashing)

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.460
- Oh, going from upside down.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.510
- [Joe] Very nicely done.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.310
- When you're changing position like that,

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.750
the blood flow is going to your brain,

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.220
then it's going to your
feet, to your brain.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.699
That could be really disorienting.

00:03:43.699 --> 00:03:45.300
- [Woman] You got it, we're not losing.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.133
- We're not losing.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.810
This poor dude is getting drowned

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.370
with bull nuts in his mouth.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.363
Only in America.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.273
- Go!

00:03:53.273 --> 00:03:54.106
- So what are they drinking?

00:03:54.106 --> 00:03:54.939
Tomato juice?

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:55.772
- [Ludacris] Habanero.

00:03:55.772 --> 00:03:57.060
- Oh, spicy sauce.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.320
- All in there, all in
there, all in there.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.220
- Oh, did he just throw up?

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.590
- It tastes like Jean-Claude
Van Damme punched me

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.423
in my throat.

00:04:02.423 --> 00:04:03.256
(record scratching)

00:04:03.256 --> 00:04:05.520
- Jean-Claude Van Damme got
his butt kicked in real life.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.680
At least do like Chuck
Norris or something.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.170
- [Ludacris] Oh, he picked all
really, really hot peppers.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.003
Come on, baby.

00:04:11.003 --> 00:04:11.836
So this is gonna hurt.

00:04:11.836 --> 00:04:14.310
- [Man] As soon as it got
in my throat, I felt it.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.480
- The capsaicin right there,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.430
is just bounding to the receptors,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.220
making it feel like burning
damage is happening.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.590
You're getting full-on
inflammatory response,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.041
swelling, sweating.

00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:25.020
Ah!

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:25.853
- [Man] I can't let him down,

00:04:25.853 --> 00:04:29.190
but my body isn't gonna
agree with what's going on.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.300
- Yeah, it's not gonna agree.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.133
And you know what?

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.823
It's gonna burn on the way out too.

00:04:34.069 --> 00:04:35.190
(gun bangs)

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.380
Oh look, there's Bear.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.850
(dog barking)

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.381
Oh, that's a scary challenge.

00:04:40.381 --> 00:04:42.089
(beep)

00:04:42.089 --> 00:04:43.375
Oh my God.

00:04:43.375 --> 00:04:44.208
(woman groaning)

00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:46.830
I assume that's a puncture proof vest,

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.360
but you would still feel the pressure

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.620
and get severe bruising.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.369
You could even fracture a bone this way.

00:04:52.369 --> 00:04:53.443
(dog growling)

00:04:53.443 --> 00:04:56.980
- [Woman] Stop, it hurts.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:57.836
- You made it through!

00:04:57.836 --> 00:04:58.669
- Did she make?

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:01.440
That was the worst anti-climatic ending.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.520
You made it through!

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.990
She almost lost her arm.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:04.881
Bear.

00:05:04.881 --> 00:05:07.800
Oh! Right in the bull testicle.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.350
Would you ever bite a
person's arm like that?

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.360
I would never do that.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.240
- [Joe] Safety officer will
release a canister of gas.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.130
You must see how long you
can stay in the building.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.420
- Interesting, tear gas.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.820
Okay, so most tear gas isn't actually gas.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.580
It's like aerosolized solids or liquids,

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.710
that cause maximal irritation.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.880
It's like, bromo-something,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.030
that cause mucus membrane
disruption, nausea,

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.260
visual changes.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.690
There's actually long-lasting
effects to tear gas.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.471
That's why they really
try and avoid using it.

00:05:35.471 --> 00:05:36.450
(woman coughing)

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.873
Yeah, it's very irritating to the airways.

00:05:39.873 --> 00:05:40.706
(woman spitting)

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:42.900
(woman coughing)
Oh, that's gonna hurt, ugh.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.730
You could have a full on asthma attack,

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.770
respiratory distress.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.410
Oh, she's gonna need to get washed.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.210
She could throw up, it doesn't end there.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:54.213
Like she needs to take a
full decontamination shower.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.550
- [Ludacris] One of you will be strapped

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.990
into this electric chair.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.553
- Okay, why?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.010
- Four of the five keys

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:05.437
inside that valet box unlocks
a restraint on this chair,

00:06:05.437 --> 00:06:06.360
(chains clinking)

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.440
freeing your partner.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.280
- And if you don't,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.140
please don't tell me you get electrocuted.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.510
- [Ludacris] If you hit
the sides of this fence,

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.950
you will be electrocuted.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.660
- Oh my God, is it like Operation?

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.310
The dark version of Operation?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.610
By the way, electrocuted
used to mean electricity

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.600
and executed.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.180
So I really hope no one
dies on Fear Factor.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.710
- Every 15 to 20 seconds,

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.090
the person inside of this chair,

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.530
will be electrocuted as well.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.080
- Stop saying electrocuted,
just say tased.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.250
Electricity is dangerous.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.240
It can stop the heart.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.440
It could cause the heart to fibrillate,

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.850
which is not a useful rhythm.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.130
You could actually get skin
burns from electricity.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.920
So it really depends on
the amount of current,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.330
how high the voltage is,

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.490
how long it's being
passed through your body.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.560
Also depends if your skin is wet or dry.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.706
Like all those things matter.

00:06:48.706 --> 00:06:53.517
- (screaming) Oh my God!

00:06:53.517 --> 00:06:55.110
- And she got tattoos before.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.700
So you know she can handle some pain.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.530
- [Joe] In that tank are electric eels,

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:00.450
containing over a thousand volts.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.190
Grab six electric eels,

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.410
and transfer them over to
the other side of the tank.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.210
You gotta hold them eels?

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.760
Medically, I don't know if this is okay.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.407
Like if my patient said, "Doctor,
I'm here to get clearance

00:07:11.407 --> 00:07:13.560
"in order to touch eels
with my bare hands."

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.441
I would say, "Please leave
for my office right now."

00:07:16.441 --> 00:07:17.336
(water splashing)

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.758
- [Joe] You just gotta commit.

00:07:18.758 --> 00:07:20.154
- Guys, I'm committing.

00:07:20.154 --> 00:07:21.060
I haven't even-
(woman screams)

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.230
- This is awkward.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.160
- You're just a big baby.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.630
- He should touch one.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:25.470
- I wanna feel it.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.320
- Go ahead, grab the big fat one.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.153
Don't touch it.

00:07:29.153 --> 00:07:30.797
- Whoa!

00:07:30.797 --> 00:07:31.917
- What did I tell you?

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:32.955
Grab it.
- That sucks.

00:07:32.955 --> 00:07:35.879
- (laughs) He learned his lesson.

00:07:35.879 --> 00:07:37.145
- 30? Is it 30?

00:07:37.145 --> 00:07:38.827
- [Joe] Let's go, you got plenty on you.

00:07:38.827 --> 00:07:39.930
Come on over.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.760
Now he's gotta suck 30 leeches off you,

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.353
before you each eat 10 of them.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:45.863
One.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.083
Two.

00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:49.290
- Ew!

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.970
You know, people used to do leech therapy.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.160
And there are some things
leeches are not terrible for,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.200
like so when leeches attach to you,

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.580
they release a chemical,

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.290
that prevents clotting from happening,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.760
cause they wanna keep sucking your blood.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.730
So that chemical can actually be utilized

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.020
for certain conditions.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.720
I don't recommend using
leech therapy on your own.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.630
It's more for scientific
research purposes.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.463
- [Joe] Hurry up!

00:08:10.463 --> 00:08:11.296
- You know, what's funny?

00:08:11.296 --> 00:08:12.129
I'm acting grossed out by this,

00:08:12.129 --> 00:08:14.640
but this is usually how
I spend my Friday nights.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.680
Sorry, Thursday nights (laughs).

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.940
What'd you do last night?

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.190
Suck some leeches off of my partner.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.023
What'd you do?

00:08:21.023 --> 00:08:21.930
Oh, did you guys have dinner first?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.460
No, I ate dinner after.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:24.870
The leeches.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.740
- [Man] When I was laying in the tub

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:26.573
(rats squeaking)

00:08:26.573 --> 00:08:28.800
with hundreds of rats
crawling all over me.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.390
- I wanna know, because I'm a doctor,

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:31.620
and I didn't learn this in school.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.510
What's the difference
between a mouse and a rat?

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.350
- [Man] Rats are bigger.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.060
- Oh, what if you have a big mouse?

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:36.893
Like, look.

00:08:36.893 --> 00:08:38.190
Look how big this mouse is.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.123
Is this a rat?

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.540
Sorry, I had to do that.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:42.660
(laughing)

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.710
- [Man] Thanks for apologizing.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.370
- I felt every single
foot of all those rats.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:48.630
Oh my God!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.720
- But rats do transfer a lot of diseases.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.360
Leptospirosis, hantavirus.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.500
So many issues.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.333
Salmonella.

00:08:56.333 --> 00:08:58.050
Like the bacteria lists are huge.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.070
Bubonic plague.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.540
How did that happen back in the day?

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.830
Rats!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.380
- [Man] Can't believe I'm
gonna have to be chained up,

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.750
while seeing my brother suffocating.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.860
I hope he doesn't freak out.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:08.693
- Hold on a second.

00:09:08.693 --> 00:09:10.080
Did they just escalate this

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.150
and make this 10 times more difficult?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.340
Just going into an enclosed
environment like that,

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.010
would instantly trigger
claustrophobia in most people.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.780
Claustrophobia is a specific phobia.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:19.980
A lot of people have that.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.350
Your symptoms will be
like, nervousness, anxiety,

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.970
all the way up to having a panic attack.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:24.960
And having a panic attack,

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.550
for those who's had them,

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.840
basically feels like the world is ending.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.100
You can't take a deep breath.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.990
Your heart's racing all over the place.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.580
- [Ludacris] One minute
30 seconds is gone.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.410
- You know, when there's
a stampede at a mall

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:35.670
or sporting event?

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.560
The real danger is like
putting pressure on your chest,

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:38.670
so much so that you can't breathe.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.380
That's what I feel like is
about to happen, right now.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:41.213
- [Man] This is like my
worst fear and like--

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:42.046
- Oh my God.

00:09:42.046 --> 00:09:43.913
He's like a human condom right now.

00:09:43.913 --> 00:09:45.477
- Hey! All right, okay.

00:09:45.477 --> 00:09:46.310
(chains clinking)

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.613
- So what happens?

00:09:47.613 --> 00:09:49.863
- [Woman] Get your brother!

00:09:51.887 --> 00:09:54.810
- Did he just do chest
compressions on him?

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.490
He's alive, you don't need to do that.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.990
These are superworms.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.940
I think superworms are actually edible.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:01.920
And they like contain some decent protein.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:02.760
Oh, there was an article,

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.070
in the New York Times not too
long ago with super worms,

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.830
because they can actually
digest styrofoam and plastic,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.310
and maybe they're a solution
to our recycling dilemma.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:14.700
It's not what I thought I would
talk about on Fear Factor.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:17.221
Someone's gonna be
power-lifting after this.

00:10:17.221 --> 00:10:18.382
(squelching)

00:10:18.382 --> 00:10:20.575
- Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

00:10:20.575 --> 00:10:22.500
- [Ludacris] Here we go, and time!

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.270
- This show is disgusting.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.160
Sadists have created this show.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.350
And somehow all of America tuned in.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.630
- [Joe] You're each gonna
have to walk barefoot,

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.860
on this broken glass.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.630
- See, this is more of a mental thing.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.490
So the thing with broken glass is,

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:36.330
I'm gonna give tips.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.750
Ideally, you do this with
wine or champagne bottle,

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.010
because it's more curved,

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:42.150
and more gentle, the glass,

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:44.730
than like if you were to use
glass from a drinking glass.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.620
And also, because there's so much glass,

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.690
the smaller particles kinda fall through

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.280
and allow a sinking sensation.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.113
So when you step,

00:10:51.113 --> 00:10:53.913
it's not as bad as stepping
on one piece of glass.

00:10:55.057 --> 00:10:58.230
(glass clinking)

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.970
Most people don't even cut their feet,

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.508
if you're doing it correctly.

00:11:01.508 --> 00:11:04.020
(glass clinking)

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.190
Yeah, see he's doing the right thing.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.170
He's like separating the
glass to get the edges off.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:08.370
- [Joe] Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.600
Lift your foot up.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.980
- [Man] Ah, see it's
putting it right in my foot.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.540
- He walked across all this glass,

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.950
and it only started to hurt

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:15.840
when he stepped on one piece of glass.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.460
- Our strategy is for me

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.402
to try to eat most of the marshmallows.

00:11:19.402 --> 00:11:20.235
(beep)

00:11:20.235 --> 00:11:21.450
(buzzing)

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.290
- What is the marshmallow?

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.150
It's a marshmallow covered by bees?

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.560
At first, challenge seems doable.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.120
Then you realize the
marshmallows they have to eat,

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.470
are covered in live flies.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:29.400
Flies are gross,

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.500
because not only do
they like land on poop,

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.580
and then land on your food,

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.080
who knows where these flies have been.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.070
Do you know how flies eat?

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:36.630
Like if they land on your watermelon,

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.300
flies puke on your watermelon first,

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.400
in order to get their
enzymes into the food.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.567
(gagging)

00:11:46.528 --> 00:11:47.910
I came so close to throwing up there.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:48.750
My eyes are watering.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.160
How are they eating that?

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.510
I mean, the flies are just protein.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:52.343
So it's fine.

00:11:52.343 --> 00:11:55.230
It just like society has
ingrained this into my mind.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.270
Oh my God, my eyes are watering.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.160
- [Ludacris] Devin is
two marshmallows down.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.583
And Tiona ate one, so five more to go.

00:12:00.583 --> 00:12:03.093
- (coughs) I'm not faking this.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.760
Stop showing the zoom-ins.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.410
I'm trying to give you
medical information,

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.960
but all I can think about
is not puking right now.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:13.230
The FDA allows some pretty
shocking things in your food.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.430
Click here to check that out.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:15.840
As always stay happy and healthy.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:17.550
This list will surprise you.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.480
Like it surprised me what the FDA said.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.550
Yeah, that's in there.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.862
Cool. What?

00:12:21.862 --> 00:12:24.445
(upbeat music)

